[{:db/id "0cad4500-905a-5858-8c3f-a7b60b352b59" :answer/id #uuid "0cad4500-905a-5858-8c3f-a7b60b352b59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "026784b9-3bc0-5798-b8b5-2ea62f5c5f83" :answer/id #uuid "026784b9-3bc0-5798-b8b5-2ea62f5c5f83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8e67acde-888e-5817-a582-ac7742afc991" :answer/id #uuid "8e67acde-888e-5817-a582-ac7742afc991" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2eb01dae-041f-5459-8b96-b3482e964c0f" :answer/id #uuid "2eb01dae-041f-5459-8b96-b3482e964c0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f8da406d-b2dc-5b56-b3c5-186cce25d980" :answer/id #uuid "f8da406d-b2dc-5b56-b3c5-186cce25d980" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "11f6bfad-4fb4-53b7-b7e6-318260e0f958" :answer-field/id #uuid "11f6bfad-4fb4-53b7-b7e6-318260e0f958" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["0cad4500-905a-5858-8c3f-a7b60b352b59" "026784b9-3bc0-5798-b8b5-2ea62f5c5f83" "8e67acde-888e-5817-a582-ac7742afc991" "2eb01dae-041f-5459-8b96-b3482e964c0f" "f8da406d-b2dc-5b56-b3c5-186cce25d980"] :answer-field/correct "8e67acde-888e-5817-a582-ac7742afc991" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "b24cc741-a0e1-52fd-84de-966d881c283d" :question/id #uuid "b24cc741-a0e1-52fd-84de-966d881c283d" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7bd61d778e3ea17a10adad21dd63cfae068af48700e6217194bb48e995c9f6e7.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the circle shown above. What is ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A$ expressed in polar coordinates?\n\nChoose a change-of-variables setup with $r\\geq0$ that describes $D$ and the transformed integrand, including the Jacobian." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA={∬}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents the disk of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta):0\\leq r\\leq \\sqrt{2},\\ 0\\leq\\theta\\leq 2 \\pi\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}-(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2})r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["11f6bfad-4fb4-53b7-b7e6-318260e0f958"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "b12e0871-185b-543d-bc3b-20afa90aead8" :answer/id #uuid "b12e0871-185b-543d-bc3b-20afa90aead8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(r+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "56407af4-1fb7-53b1-86b8-13243e6095fc" :answer/id #uuid "56407af4-1fb7-53b1-86b8-13243e6095fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "490bf319-a19a-5705-874f-041fecb63bc4" :answer/id #uuid "490bf319-a19a-5705-874f-041fecb63bc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "71005229-4609-51a5-b252-aec7c9944620" :answer/id #uuid "71005229-4609-51a5-b252-aec7c9944620" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5d545206-ca9c-5b98-9471-863533f19aca" :answer/id #uuid "5d545206-ca9c-5b98-9471-863533f19aca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(r+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "51400ed4-9db0-5c43-83b2-f1b92948e695" :answer-field/id #uuid "51400ed4-9db0-5c43-83b2-f1b92948e695" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["b12e0871-185b-543d-bc3b-20afa90aead8" "56407af4-1fb7-53b1-86b8-13243e6095fc" "490bf319-a19a-5705-874f-041fecb63bc4" "71005229-4609-51a5-b252-aec7c9944620" "5d545206-ca9c-5b98-9471-863533f19aca"] :answer-field/correct "71005229-4609-51a5-b252-aec7c9944620" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "f6d7b368-d715-54c1-b3b0-bf00daf35574" :question/id #uuid "f6d7b368-d715-54c1-b3b0-bf00daf35574" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7bd61d778e3ea17a10adad21dd63cfae068af48700e6217194bb48e995c9f6e7.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the circle shown above. What is ${∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}A$ expressed in polar coordinates?\n\nChoose a change-of-variables setup with $r\\geq0$ that describes $D$ and the transformed integrand, including the Jacobian." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA={∬}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents the disk of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta):0\\leq r\\leq \\sqrt{2},\\ 0\\leq\\theta\\leq 2 \\pi\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\operatorname{ln}⁡((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+1)r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+1)\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r\\operatorname{ln}⁡({r}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["51400ed4-9db0-5c43-83b2-f1b92948e695"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "33180dbf-afc0-5cf5-a045-d20f9c205b3f" :answer/id #uuid "33180dbf-afc0-5cf5-a045-d20f9c205b3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{3} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "266130f7-fe7a-555d-8bc3-c644a951aa45" :answer/id #uuid "266130f7-fe7a-555d-8bc3-c644a951aa45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a958bcf2-9156-5ac1-892f-0a551baa748b" :answer/id #uuid "a958bcf2-9156-5ac1-892f-0a551baa748b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "eb76449e-7e26-50e6-90fa-e3ea350c8e4b" :answer/id #uuid "eb76449e-7e26-50e6-90fa-e3ea350c8e4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{5} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d0307e5f-4a08-5149-9fb2-d9fdd6da4411" :answer/id #uuid "d0307e5f-4a08-5149-9fb2-d9fdd6da4411" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "416649c6-1d29-50f8-997b-94939fdfa192" :answer-field/id #uuid "416649c6-1d29-50f8-997b-94939fdfa192" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["33180dbf-afc0-5cf5-a045-d20f9c205b3f" "266130f7-fe7a-555d-8bc3-c644a951aa45" "a958bcf2-9156-5ac1-892f-0a551baa748b" "eb76449e-7e26-50e6-90fa-e3ea350c8e4b" "d0307e5f-4a08-5149-9fb2-d9fdd6da4411"] :answer-field/correct "d0307e5f-4a08-5149-9fb2-d9fdd6da4411" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "65d15c33-14f0-5a8d-980c-cdd3dc5eab53" :question/id #uuid "65d15c33-14f0-5a8d-980c-cdd3dc5eab53" :question/problem "![](images/b4/b4a332a1bea58e47ab58fa47c6944213ce4caa5d26e6bfb129fea613adcd524b.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the quarter-circle shown above. What is $\\iint_D 2 x y \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}A$ expressed in polar coordinates?\n\nChoose a change-of-variables setup with $r\\geq0$ that describes $D$ and the transformed integrand, including the Jacobian." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iint_D f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A=\\iint_\\Delta f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)\\,r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta),$ the region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta):0\\leq r\\leq \\sqrt{2},\\ 0\\leq\\theta\\leq \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nSince $r\\geq0$, $\\sqrt{r^2}=r$; also $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$.\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D 2 x y \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}A&=\\iint_\\Delta 2 (r\\cos\\theta) (r\\sin\\theta) \\sqrt{(r\\cos\\theta)^{2} + (r\\sin\\theta)^{2}}\\,r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}2r^3\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta\\sqrt{r^2(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}2r^4\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^4\\sin(2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["416649c6-1d29-50f8-997b-94939fdfa192"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "3b07f7ba-836e-561a-b89e-43ec179cff33" :answer/id #uuid "3b07f7ba-836e-561a-b89e-43ec179cff33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{3} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c81d2b5f-e76b-538a-a273-bbf8662e4bad" :answer/id #uuid "c81d2b5f-e76b-538a-a273-bbf8662e4bad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "006f8cc3-fe44-506e-abc5-5bcc0cdda89d" :answer/id #uuid "006f8cc3-fe44-506e-abc5-5bcc0cdda89d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d42cb897-fc52-56c1-aaa4-b8bdafde567b" :answer/id #uuid "d42cb897-fc52-56c1-aaa4-b8bdafde567b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{5} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "41705678-4952-599d-819d-ab0c479baa66" :answer/id #uuid "41705678-4952-599d-819d-ab0c479baa66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "20e8a619-79f2-5c97-8bf1-deb805b2a8ed" :answer-field/id #uuid "20e8a619-79f2-5c97-8bf1-deb805b2a8ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["3b07f7ba-836e-561a-b89e-43ec179cff33" "c81d2b5f-e76b-538a-a273-bbf8662e4bad" "006f8cc3-fe44-506e-abc5-5bcc0cdda89d" "d42cb897-fc52-56c1-aaa4-b8bdafde567b" "41705678-4952-599d-819d-ab0c479baa66"] :answer-field/correct "41705678-4952-599d-819d-ab0c479baa66" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "dbec5b4a-692d-58b4-b3b1-bed97fa7c019" :question/id #uuid "dbec5b4a-692d-58b4-b3b1-bed97fa7c019" :question/problem "![](images/b4/b4a332a1bea58e47ab58fa47c6944213ce4caa5d26e6bfb129fea613adcd524b.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the quarter-circle shown above. What is $\\iint_D \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right) \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}A$ expressed in polar coordinates?\n\nChoose a change-of-variables setup with $r\\geq0$ that describes $D$ and the transformed integrand, including the Jacobian." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iint_D f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A=\\iint_\\Delta f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)\\,r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta),$ the region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta):0\\leq r\\leq \\sqrt{2},\\ 0\\leq\\theta\\leq \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nSince $r\\geq0$, $\\sqrt{r^2}=r$; also $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$.\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right) \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}A&=\\iint_\\Delta \\left((r\\cos\\theta)^{2} - (r\\sin\\theta)^{2}\\right) \\sqrt{(r\\cos\\theta)^{2} + (r\\sin\\theta)^{2}}\\,r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^3(\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta)\\sqrt{r^2(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^4(\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^4\\cos(2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["20e8a619-79f2-5c97-8bf1-deb805b2a8ed"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "def0eed0-b0f4-542a-9f44-1d63a9047258" :answer/id #uuid "def0eed0-b0f4-542a-9f44-1d63a9047258" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{3} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "67e550be-2618-51a5-b473-ae78444d24d1" :answer/id #uuid "67e550be-2618-51a5-b473-ae78444d24d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "74e8cc33-262d-54d0-9d13-a5424bcf12e0" :answer/id #uuid "74e8cc33-262d-54d0-9d13-a5424bcf12e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9424c60b-ac35-5ce4-87fb-8d2efb4c4191" :answer/id #uuid "9424c60b-ac35-5ce4-87fb-8d2efb4c4191" :answer/type :a